#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:5
#: e5c3839a20604d0da1f8ec27f77f8210
msgid "EKF Failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:7
#: b571e05006634e2a9fe763fbb182d1c3
msgid "The EKF failsafe monitors the health of EKF (the position and attitude estimation system) to catch problems with the vehicle's position estimate (caused by compass errors or velocity estimate errors) and prevent \"swimaways\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:10
#: 56b553f4d82048ec884b5dbd89c9b7fd
msgid "When will it trigger?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:12
#: 8db924a978d84f90b64ba1cf9ae0448d
msgid "The EKF failsafe will trigger when any two of the EKF \"variances\" for compass, position or velocity are higher than the :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` parameter value for 1 second."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:14
#: 5ca507fe5cc64e36a6b8f850c3b63576
msgid "These \"variances\" come from the EKF itself and are numbers indicating the EKF's confidence in its estimates.  The values are between 0 and 1 with 0 meaning the estimate is very trustworthy and 1.0 is very untrustworthy."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:16
#: 312216acec824f5090e91bdcd0db231e
msgid "The EKF calculates these \"variances\" by comparing the results from multiple sensors.  So for example, if the GPS position suddenly jumps but the accelerometers do not show a sudden acceleration, the EKF variance for position would climb (i.e become less trustworthy)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:18
#: d204055c4e0c41d49255b4610b28c734
msgid "The variances can be viewed in real-time on the ground station.  If using Mission Planner click on the \"EKF\" label on the HUD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:25
#: 1554e1466fe54b30b8118e1b44ec07ad
msgid "What will happen when the failsafe triggers?"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:27
#: 43757bc72eff40f682346ab08a623e1b
msgid "The autopilot's `LED will flash red-yellow or blue-yellow and the tone-alarm will sound <https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=j-CMLrAwlco&feature=player_detailpage&t=60s>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:28
#: 2e6eb088597c469d9d4a129acd11c3a1
msgid "\"EKF variance\" will appear on the ground station's HUD if telemetry is connected"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:29
#: 945f6e25f87b46a09b0714df2ab054dd
msgid "In manual flight modes that do not require position (i.e. Stabilize, Acro, AltHold) nothing further will happen but the pilot will be unable to switch into autonomous flight modes (PosHold, Guided, Auto) until the failure clears"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:30
#: a4c8ea904c2645dc9fc012bdde362302
msgid "In autonomous modes that require position (i.e. PosHold, Guided, Auto, etc) the :ref:`FS_EKF_ACTION <FS_EKF_ACTION>` controls the behaviour.  By default this is \"0\" meaning the vehicle will take no action. \"1\" will send a GCS warning message. \"2\" will Disarm the sub."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:31
#: 85d668f323fc4c35b468ac87b5c75dc6
msgid "An EKF failsafe error will be written to the dataflash logs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:33
#: fdc62cd577f74cf39ec113adb1c340be
msgid "After an EKF failsafe occurs, the pilot can re-take control (using the flight mode switch) in a manual flight mode such as :ref:`AltHold <altholdmode>` to bring the vehicle home."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:36
#: bbbb73daeebb4f3ebac3820bc4a121b5
msgid "Adjusting the Sensitivity of the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:38
#: 0a3ec17710e844f4859278febe9b51a4
msgid "The :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` parameter can be adjusted to control the sensitivity of the failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:40
#: 24bef042c52442c49db2eee9d198b1e0
msgid "Set :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` = 0 to disable the EKF failsafe"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:41
#: 1f39f9e8007b45e8992c9833e2c0e3e2
msgid "Increase :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` to values between 0.8 and 1.0 to reduce the chance of an EKF failsafe.  The downside of increasing this parameter value is that during a flyaway caused by a bad compass or positioning glitch, the vehicle will swim further away before the failsafe is activated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/ekf-inav-failsafe.rst:42
#: 1923762790964008aab40a17eff23806
msgid "Decrease :ref:`FS_EKF_THRESH <FS_EKF_THRESH>` to values as low as 0.6 to increase the chance of an EKF failsafe triggering quickly.  The downside of lowering this value is the EKF failsafe could trigger during aggressive maneuvers"
msgstr ""
